(1. PURPOSE, CONTRACT STRUCTURE AND PRECEDENCE) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(This master wording defines the common coverage rules for the fictional Corporate Standard) Tj
T*
(Plan. It must be read with the benefit schedule, endorsements and member certificate.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-1.1  Policy components) Tj
T*
(   The contract set consists of the signed policy schedule, member certificate,) Tj
T*
(   endorsements, this master wording, the benefit schedule and accepted proposal) Tj
T*
(   information. Operational guides explain procedures but cannot enlarge or reduce cover.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-1.2  Order of precedence) Tj
T*
(   A signed endorsement prevails over the policy schedule only for the subject it amends.) Tj
T*
(   The policy schedule prevails over this wording. This wording prevails over member guides) Tj
T*
(   and internal procedures. A later effective version prevails only for claims occurring) Tj
T*
(   during that version period.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-1.3  Evidence-based interpretation) Tj
T*
(   No benefit is payable merely because a treatment is medically useful. Payment requires) Tj
T*
(   eligibility, an active cover period, an insured benefit, medical necessity, required) Tj
T*
(   evidence, and absence of an applicable exclusion or limit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-1.4  No silent assumptions) Tj
T*
(   If member identity, plan, effective date, diagnosis, procedure, provider, or policy) Tj
T*
(   evidence is uncertain, the claim must be marked PENDING_INFORMATION or MANUAL_REVIEW) Tj
T*
(   rather than accepted or rejected by inference.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
