(3. CORE HOSPITALIZATION COVER) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(This section defines the principal insured event.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-3.1  In-patient hospitalization) Tj
T*
(   Reasonable and customary expenses are eligible when the member is admitted for at least) Tj
T*
(   twenty-four consecutive hours for medically necessary treatment on written advice of a) Tj
T*
(   registered medical practitioner.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-3.2  Day-care procedures) Tj
T*
(   The twenty-four-hour requirement does not apply to listed or clinically established) Tj
T*
(   day-care procedures requiring hospital infrastructure because technological advancement) Tj
T*
(   permits earlier discharge.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-3.3  Covered expense categories) Tj
T*
(   Subject to the schedule, eligible costs include room, nursing, ICU, surgeon,) Tj
T*
(   anaesthetist, physician, diagnostic tests, medicines, implants, operation theatre and) Tj
T*
(   medically necessary consumables that are not expressly non-payable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-3.4  Medical necessity) Tj
T*
(   The diagnosis, setting, duration and intensity of care must be consistent with generally) Tj
T*
(   accepted clinical practice. Experimental convenience or provider preference alone does) Tj
T*
(   not establish medical necessity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-3.5  Reasonable and customary charge) Tj
T*
(   The payable charge may be limited to the usual charge for comparable treatment, provider) Tj
T*
(   class and locality. Any reduction must identify the benchmark and affected line item.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-3.6  Emergency stabilization) Tj
T*
(   Emergency stabilization is covered when delay would reasonably threaten life, limb or) Tj
T*
(   organ function. Network authorization requirements may be relaxed, but notification and) Tj
T*
(   evidence requirements still apply as soon as practicable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
