(4. ASSOCIATED BENEFITS) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(These benefits apply only when shown as active in AIEHBP-BEN-002.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-4.1  Pre-hospitalization) Tj
T*
(   Medical expenses incurred during the thirty days immediately before an admissible) Tj
T*
(   hospitalization are eligible when directly related to the same condition.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-4.2  Post-hospitalization) Tj
T*
(   Medical expenses incurred during the sixty days immediately after discharge are eligible) Tj
T*
(   when directly related to the same condition and supported by prescriptions and invoices.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-4.3  Road ambulance) Tj
T*
(   Emergency road ambulance charges to the nearest suitable hospital are payable up to the) Tj
T*
(   schedule limit when medically necessary.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-4.4  AYUSH hospitalization) Tj
T*
(   In-patient treatment under Ayurveda, Yoga and Naturopathy, Unani, Siddha or Homeopathy is) Tj
T*
(   eligible only at a recognized facility and subject to the same necessity and) Tj
T*
(   documentation standards.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-4.5  Organ donor expenses) Tj
T*
(   Hospitalization expenses of an organ donor may be eligible when the recipient is an) Tj
T*
(   insured member and the transplant claim is admissible. Organ acquisition, trafficking,) Tj
T*
(   donor screening unrelated to an approved transplant and donor follow-up are not covered) Tj
T*
(   unless listed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-4.6  Domiciliary treatment) Tj
T*
(   Home treatment is eligible only when hospitalization would otherwise be required but) Tj
T*
(   transfer is impossible or hospital accommodation is unavailable, and daily clinical) Tj
T*
(   records are supplied.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
