(7. CLAIMS DUTIES AND DECISION STATES) Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
(Procedural duties support timely assessment but must be applied fairly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-7.1  Notification) Tj
T*
(   Planned admissions require preauthorization before admission. Emergency admissions should) Tj
T*
(   be notified within twenty-four hours or as soon as reasonably possible.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-7.2  Reimbursement submission) Tj
T*
(   A reimbursement claim should be submitted within thirty days after discharge unless the) Tj
T*
(   schedule or law provides a different period. Delay supported by reasonable cause must be) Tj
T*
(   reviewed rather than automatically rejected.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-7.3  Cooperation) Tj
T*
(   The member must provide accurate information, authorization to obtain relevant records) Tj
T*
(   and reasonable assistance with verification.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-7.4  Decision states) Tj
T*
(   Permitted workflow states are RECEIVED, PENDING_INFORMATION, UNDER_MEDICAL_REVIEW,) Tj
T*
(   APPROVED, PARTIALLY_APPROVED, REJECTED, WITHDRAWN and MANUAL_REVIEW.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(POL-7.5  Reasoned decision) Tj
T*
(   Every reduction or rejection must cite the controlling clause, explain facts relied upon,) Tj
T*
(   show the calculation where relevant, and describe review or grievance options.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
endstream
